/*
 * =============================================================================
 * Xaloqi Zephyr-Reference-ECU
 * boards/nucleo_h753zi_canfd.overlay
 *
 * Added by -DDIAG_CAN_FD=ON (CMakeLists.txt), after nucleo_h753zi.overlay:
 * the CAN FD data phase of FDCAN1 for the Pi 5 CAN FD bench. The arbitration
 * phase stays 500 kbit/s at 87.5 %, so the bus, the IDs and the classic-CAN
 * tester settings are unchanged.
 *
 * Data phase: 2 Mbit/s at 80 %.
 *  - FDCAN1's kernel clock is PLL2Q = 8 MHz HSE / 4 * 120 / 3 = 80 MHz
 *    (nucleo_h753zi board DT, FDCAN_SEL), so 2 Mbit/s is 40 tq with prescaler
 *    1, and 80 % is exact. Zephyr's m_can driver turns on transmitter delay
 *    compensation by itself at that prescaler.
 *  - The Waveshare 2-CH CAN FD HAT (MCP2518FD, 40 MHz) gets 20 tq at 2 Mbit/s,
 *    80 % exact too: DomD's `ip link set canX ... dbitrate 2000000
 *    dsample-point 0.8 fd on`.
 *  - 2 Mbit/s, not more: the transceiver on this end has to be FD-rated (the
 *    SN65HVD230 is specified to 1 Mbit/s), and a bench of jumper wire and screw
 *    terminals is not a characterised harness. 5 Mbit/s (16 tq here, 8 tq on
 *    the MCP2518FD) is the next step once 2 Mbit/s runs clean.
 *
 * This ECU does not set BRS on what it sends (tp->brs stays false, src/main.c;
 * EDS v1.27.0 can, via can.fd_brs), so this data phase is used for frames the
 * ECU receives; its own FD frames go at 500 kbit/s.
 * =============================================================================
 */

&fdcan1 {
	bitrate-data      = <2000000>;
	sample-point-data = <800>;
};
